## Migrations (Alembic)

Schema changes are managed with Alembic. `migrations/env.py` reads `DATABASE_URL` from
your settings at run time and targets `app.db.models.Base.metadata`, so autogenerate sees
every mapped table.

```bash
just migration "describe the change"   # alembic revision --autogenerate -m ...
just migrate                           # alembic upgrade head
```

{% if include_tenancy or include_rbac %}Initial migrations for the `items` + `user` tables and the
`organizations` + `memberships` tables ship in `migrations/versions/` — run `just migrate`
to create them.{% elif include_users %}An initial migration for the `items` + `user` tables ships in
`migrations/versions/` — run `just migrate` to create them.{% else %}`migrations/versions/`
starts empty: generate your first migration with `just migration "initial schema"`,
review it, then `just migrate`.{% endif %}

